 "reading": "Across 37 chains (34 of them with a physically formed disulfide) the attack angle spans 131.9-146.8 deg and reaches the 150 deg backside floor in none of them, the attack site is occupied in all of them, and backbone is among the occupants in 37. What does NOT replicate is which residue occupies the site: it is the Thr116 and Val118 side chains in the 2C9U conformer the single-chain measurement used, and Gly147 backbone in most chains of 7FB9 and in the other 2C9U conformer. The occupancy is a property of the fold and the occupant is a property of the conformer, so a claim about the obstruction should rest on the first. 7FB9 is 2.70 A with its S-S distances refinement-restrained, which makes it strong evidence on the angle and the backbone and weak evidence on side-chain identity.",
