  "reading": "SOD1 has four cysteines and two of them are the bond, so Cys6 and Cys111 are the only possible attackers and there is no third cysteine left to act as the relay that reaches the buried disulfide in pI258 arsenate reductase (Messens et al., JMB 2004). Both ends are tested because a relay may attack either sulfur. All four routes fail, for two different reasons: the approaches to Cys57 are far and nowhere near collinear, and the approaches to Cys146 are either close and misaligned (Cys6) or well aligned and twice as far (Cys111)."
